-  "body": "<h2 id=\"availability\">Live testing</h2><p>Deployed October 23 for live testing. Automated native, content and cache checks passed. Full encounters, client-visible behavior and owner balance acceptance remain open.</p><h2 id=\"story\">Camil’s vigil</h2><p>The route starts with Camil in East Commonlands at level 50, with Paladin in any held class slot. A Keeper near Befallen in West Commonlands opens a Chapterhouse expedition. The native Tasks window tracks Sered, three memorials, Elowen’s three-wave defense, Halvyr, three bound knights, Vaelen, the Unbroken Shadow and the altar, then return to Camil.</p><h2 id=\"difficulty\">Endgame capstone</h2><p>The tuning target is a demanding fight for a fully developed level-50 character, including legal undead procs, Slay Undead, Ghoulbane and critical AAs. Reaching level 50 alone does not imply readiness. Sered rewards timely interrupts; Elowen needs protection. Vaelen and the Shadow mark your position with a three-second warning: move more than ten paces or interrupt. Undead bonuses remain effective. Full encounter balance and other strong class combinations still require player testing.</p><h2 id=\"progress\">Personal progress</h2><p>Earned chapters survive reconnects and run resets. Removing the Tasks display does not erase them. Make room for both story and dungeon journals. Eligible nearby participants earn personal credit; later witnesses cannot borrow another player’s kills. The helmet claim survives a full inventory and is delivered once.</p><h2 id=\"rewards\">Rewards</h2><p>The existing Winged Helm of the Dawn keeps its stats and sockets. Three miniboss items and final Raid designs use current level-50 dungeon budgets. Ember of the First Dawn is a type-22 armor augment with four qualities: HP/mana 60/87/114/144, heroic STA/WIS 5/6/8/10 and AC 2/3/5/6. It requires level 50 and follows existing Hunt headroom and zone forging. Static curated enemies have a 0.5% augment roll, with quality weights 60/30/8/2; miniboss custom items have a 35% roll. <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">Browse every published reward and its values</a>.</p><h2 id=\"access\">Classic access</h2><p>Chapterhouse uses a scoped exception while Classic and level 50 remain global. Its population, spells and rewards are curated; stock Rain of Fear drops are excluded. The waypoint recalls to a public foyer, and the Keeper controls private run admission.</p>",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"availability\">Live testing</h2><p>Deployed October 23 for live testing. Automated native, content and cache checks passed. Full encounters, client-visible behavior and owner balance acceptance remain open.</p><h2 id=\"story\">Camil’s vigil</h2><p>The route starts with Camil in East Commonlands at level 50, with Paladin in any held class slot. A Keeper near Befallen in West Commonlands opens a Chapterhouse expedition. The native Tasks window tracks Sered, three memorials, Elowen’s three-wave defense, Halvyr, three bound knights, Vaelen, the Unbroken Shadow and the altar, then return to Camil.</p><h2 id=\"difficulty\">Endgame capstone</h2><p>The tuning target is a demanding fight for a fully developed level-50 character, including legal undead procs, Slay Undead, Ghoulbane and critical AAs. Reaching level 50 alone does not imply readiness. Sered rewards timely interrupts; Elowen needs protection. Vaelen and the Shadow mark your position with a three-second warning: move more than ten paces or interrupt. Undead bonuses remain effective. Full encounter balance and other strong class combinations still require player testing.</p><h2 id=\"progress\">Personal progress</h2><p>Earned chapters survive reconnects and run resets. Removing the Tasks display does not erase them. Make room for both story and dungeon journals. Eligible nearby participants earn personal credit; later witnesses cannot borrow another player’s kills. The helmet claim survives a full inventory and is delivered once.</p><h2 id=\"rewards\">Rewards</h2><p>The existing Winged Helm of the Dawn keeps its stats and sockets. Three miniboss items and final Raid designs use current level-50 dungeon budgets. Ember of the First Dawn is a type-22 armor augment with four qualities: HP/mana 60/87/114/144, heroic STA/WIS 5/6/8/10 and AC 2/3/5/6. It requires level 50 and follows existing Hunt headroom and zone forging. Static curated enemies have a 0.5% augment roll, with quality weights 60/30/8/2; miniboss custom items have a 35% roll. <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">Browse every published reward and its values</a>.</p><h2 id=\"access\">Classic access</h2><p>Chapterhouse uses a scoped exception while Classic and level 50 remain global. Its population, spells and rewards are curated; stock Rain of Fear drops are excluded. The waypoint recalls to a public foyer, and the Keeper controls private run admission.</p><h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — not released</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is a prepared level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. It is not yet installed. Client appearance and complete encounters still require in-game acceptance.</p><p>This separate Shadow Knight campaign follows the Vigil’s structure. Camil’s progress and helmet entitlement remain independent.</p>",
   "slug": "camil-vigil"
 }
