@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
   "slug": "dungeon-modes",
   "title": "Raid & Grind dungeons",
   "summary": "Raid and Grind choices, Keepers, objectives and unique MAGIC rewards across 21 Classic dungeons, including Fear, Hate and Sky.",
-  "body": "<h2 id=\"hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — every Classic dungeon:</strong> The installed release extends Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset to 21 Classic combat dungeons, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 dungeons and their new rewards are installed for testing. In-game and balance acceptance are pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon — live testing</h2><p><strong>Live testing.</strong> Added zones: blackburrow, crushbone, runnyeye, soldunga, guktop, gukbottom, mistmoore, kedge, paw, hole, qcat, fearplane, hateplane, airplane. Current native populations are retained; this is not a historical restoration of every zone. Runs keep the existing twelve-hour limit and personal credit requirements.</p><p>Added Raid final bosses receive three dungeon-specific exclusive designs in Polished and Ascended versions. All dungeon rewards are MAGIC; existing item IDs and other stats remain unchanged. Managed Sky adds durable key exchangers on each key island, still requiring the normal tokens. Managed Grind gives the four previously scripted Sky bosses eight-hour timers and preserves the princess’s four-hour timer. Public and legacy Sky retain their original behavior. Plane runs isolate their quest state from public zones and other runs.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Keeper placement — live testing:</strong> The overlapping Keepers in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair now have positions 15 units from their waypoints. High Keep and Cazic-Thule already had separate positions and remain unchanged. Visibility is not yet confirmed in game. If an eye is still hidden, use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail. Waypoints and dungeon progress are unchanged.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Befallen</td><td><code>-67,35,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Unrest</td><td><code>-38,67,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Najena</td><td><code>-61,858,4.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Permafrost</td><td><code>-121,46,2.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Nagafen’s Lair</td><td><code>-424,-248,-108</code></td></tr><tr><td>High Keep (unchanged)</td><td><code>-16,88,4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cazic-Thule (unchanged)</td><td><code>71,-74,4</code></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected dungeon equipment budgets are raised so comparable Normal rewards exceed Ascended starter gear. Modes, objectives, Keepers and eligibility remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. Existing legacy runs keep their original behavior until expiry or reset. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>Raid and Grind choices are available in all 21 Classic combat dungeons listed here, including Fear, Hate and Sky. Each run lasts twelve hours and allows up to six characters. Testing and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"modes\">Choose a mode</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Grind</th><th>Raid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Enemies</td><td>Normal stats and respawns</td><td>35% more HP, 15% more damage; defeated enemies do not return</td></tr><tr><td>Bosses</td><td>Required bosses available initially</td><td>Final boss unlocks after all required minibosses</td></tr><tr><td>Personal reward</td><td>One Normal item</td><td>One item: 90% Polished, 10% Ascended</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"credit\">Earn your own checklist</h2><p>The creator chooses the mode. Hail the entrance Keeper for Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset. Open Tasks and select your dungeon and mode for its checklist and deadline. Keeper Status lists every required boss, your personal credit and permanent completion counts. A yellow Task Stage Completed message marks one boss objective. A full dungeon clear requires personal credit for every required boss. During live testing, if the task objectives are blank or Completed history is missing, use Keeper Status; these display problems do not erase earned credit or rewards. Stay enrolled, connected and within 200 units of your party’s encounter, including vertical distance. Owned-pet kills count for the owner’s party. Missed kills never receive retroactive credit. Grind respawns offer another opportunity; Raid deaths are permanent for that run.</p>\n<h2 id=\"required-bosses\">Required bosses</h2><p>Each name below is required for personal completion in either mode. The final boss is marked; Raid unlocks it after the required minibosses. A group’s unlock does not give missed personal credit.</p><h3>Befallen</h3><ul><li>skeleton Lrodd</li><li>Priest Amiaz</li><li>the thaumaturgist</li><li>Boondin Babbinsbort</li><li>Gynok Moltor — final boss</li></ul><h3>Unrest</h3><ul><li>lesser blade fiend</li><li>a reanimated hand</li><li>reclusive ghoul magus</li><li>an undead barkeep</li><li>an undead knight of Unrest</li><li>a priest of najena</li><li>Garanel Rucksif — final boss</li></ul><h3>High Keep</h3><ul><li>Captain Bosec</li><li>Captain Boshinko</li><li>Dyrna Nlith</li><li>Carson McCabe — final boss</li></ul><h3>Najena</h3><ul><li>Moosh</li><li>Ekeros</li><li>BoneCracker</li><li>Rathyl</li><li>Trazdon</li><li>Drelzna</li><li>the guard captain</li><li>The Widowmistress</li><li>Najena — final boss</li></ul><h3>Cazic-Thule</h3><ul><li>Radiant</li><li>Tae Ew Diviner</li><li>Tae Ew Templar</li><li>Tae Ew Archon</li><li>Cazic Cenobite</li><li>Avatar of Fear — final boss</li></ul><h3>Permafrost</h3><ul><li>a goblin jailmaster</li><li>a goblin preacher</li><li>a goblin scryer</li><li>the goblin sage</li><li>an elite honor guard</li><li>High Priest Zaharn</li><li>King Thex`Ka IV</li><li>Lady Vox — final boss</li></ul><h3>Nagafen’s Lair</h3><ul><li>guano harvester</li><li>kobold noble</li><li>kobold champion</li><li>kobold priest</li><li>Solusek kobold king</li><li>death beetle</li><li>noxious spider</li><li>stone spider</li><li>Efreeti Lord Djarn</li><li>Magus Rokyl</li><li>King Tranix</li><li>Warlord Skarlon</li><li>Lord Nagafen — final boss</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"added-keepers\">Additional entrance Keepers</h2><p>Use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail if its eye model is difficult to select. Locations use in-game <code>/loc</code> order. Hate’s public Keeper is in East Commonlands; its private instances retain the entrance Keeper. Each Keeper has Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blackburrow</td><td><code>-159,23,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Crushbone</td><td><code>-644,174,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Runnyeye</td><td><code>106,201,3.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Solusek&#x27;s Eye</td><td><code>-487.312,-474.688,71.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Upper Guk</td><td><code>-36,23,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Lower Guk</td><td><code>1197,-201,-81.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Mistmoore</td><td><code>-314,120,-179.938</code></td></tr><tr><td>Kedge Keep</td><td><code>100,30,301.875</code></td></tr><tr><td>Splitpaw</td><td><code>-106,63,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>The Hole</td><td><code>624,-1050,-78.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Qeynos Catacombs</td><td><code>860,96,-39.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Fear</td><td><code>-1139,1298,-0.371</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Hate (East Commonlands)</td><td><code>-1570,-346,3</code>; private Hate entrance: <code>-374.8,-337.08,2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Sky</td><td><code>1415,630,-666.709</code></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id=\"added-objectives\">Required bosses in the added dungeons</h2><p>Every listed boss requires personal credit. Raid unlocks the final boss after all required minibosses; Keeper Status is the live checklist.</p><h3>Blackburrow</h3><ul><li>a gnoll commander</li><li>Splitpaw Commander</li><li>the gnoll high shaman</li><li>Lord Elgnub — final boss</li></ul><h3>Crushbone</h3><ul><li>orc taskmaster</li><li>orc warlord</li><li>Lord Darish</li><li>The Prophet</li><li>Ambassador DVinn</li><li>Emperor Crush — final boss</li></ul><h3>Runnyeye</h3><ul><li>The Sporali Moldmaster</li><li>Sludge Dankmire</li><li>Battlelord Paluk</li><li>Battlewizard Unak</li><li>Lord Pickclaw — final boss</li></ul><h3>Solusek&#x27;s Eye</h3><ul><li>flame goblin foreman</li><li>reckless efreeti</li><li>Singe</li><li>Kindle</li><li>inferno goblin captain</li><li>goblin high shaman</li><li>Lord Gimblox</li><li>Solusek goblin king — final boss</li></ul><h3>Upper Guk</h3><ul><li>a froglok gaz squire</li><li>a giant heart spider</li><li>a froglok scryer</li><li>a froglok realist</li><li>the froglok warden</li><li>a froglok summoner</li><li>the froglok shin lord — final boss</li></ul><h3>Lower Guk</h3><ul><li>a minotaur elder</li><li>a minotaur patriarch</li><li>a ghoul supplier</li><li>a ghoul executioner</li><li>a ghoul assassin</li><li>a ghoul sage</li><li>a ghoul cavalier</li><li>a frenzied ghoul</li><li>the ghoul arch magus</li><li>the froglok king</li><li>the ghoul lord — final boss</li></ul><h3>Mistmoore</h3><ul><li>a glyphed ghoul</li><li>an avenging caitiff</li><li>a cloaked dhampyre</li><li>Butler Syncall</li><li>Maid Issis</li><li>Mynthi Davissi</li><li>Lasna Cheroon</li><li>Garton Viswin</li><li>Xicotl — final boss</li></ul><h3>Kedge Keep</h3><ul><li>a frenzied cauldron shark</li><li>a fierce impaler</li><li>Coralyn Kelpmaiden</li><li>Shellara Ebbhunter</li><li>a seahorse matriarch</li><li>a seahorse patriarch</li><li>Cauldronboil</li><li>Undertow</li><li>Priestess Auraia</li><li>Phinigel Autropos — final boss</li></ul><h3>Splitpaw</h3><ul><li>Verishe Mal Judge</li><li>Verishe Mal Executioner</li><li>Tesch Val Kadvem</li><li>Nisch Val Torash Mashk</li><li>Rosch Val L`Vlor</li><li>Tesch Val Deval`Nmak</li><li>The Ishva Mal — final boss</li></ul><h3>The Hole</h3><ul><li>Stonesoul the Unmoving</li><li>Ikurenm the Sly</li><li>Tzitzi the Crazed</li><li>Commander Yarik</li><li>Irslak the Wretched — final boss</li></ul><h3>Qeynos Catacombs</h3><ul><li>a gelatinous cube</li><li>a thug leader</li><li>a ring leader</li><li>a shark</li><li>Omorb — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Fear</h3><ul><li>Dread</li><li>Terror</li><li>Fright</li><li>a dracoliche</li><li>Cazic Thule — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Hate</h3><ul><li>Magi P`Tasa</li><li>Hand of the Maestro</li><li>Maestro of Rancor</li><li>Innoruuk — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Sky</h3><ul><li>a thunder spirit princess</li><li>Protector of Sky</li><li>Gorgalosk</li><li>Keeper of Souls</li><li>The Spiroc Guardian</li><li>The Spiroc Lord</li><li>Bazzt Zzzt</li><li>Sister of the Spire</li><li>Eye of Veeshan — final boss</li></ul><h2 id=\"unique-rewards\">Unique Classic raid rewards — live testing</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p><p>New recommended levels follow each dungeon’s equipment band. Planar items require level 46. All remain permanent, tradeable, non-LORE, zero-resale and outside existing forging recipes. The original seven exclusive families remain, with MAGIC added where needed. Already earned rewards and generated loot keep their identities.</p><p>New numeric power stays within the existing band, slot and quality budgets. Their lore is original Nightcap fiction inspired by each dungeon. Each family has Polished and Ascended versions.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon / band</th><th>Exclusive designs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>blackburrow / 20</td><td>Elgnub&#x27;s Burrowfang<br>Blackburrow Packwarden Mantle<br>Brewer&#x27;s Amber Seal</td></tr><tr><td>crushbone / 20</td><td>Crush&#x27;s Broken Scepter<br>Ambassador&#x27;s Ashen Veil<br>Liberator of the Pens</td></tr><tr><td>runnyeye / 30</td><td>Pickclaw Tunnelbreaker<br>Evil Eye Witness<br>Crown of the Pickclaw Court</td></tr><tr><td>soldunga / 40</td><td>Goblin King&#x27;s Cinderstaff<br>Firebloom Forgegrips<br>Embervault Reliquary</td></tr><tr><td>guktop / 30</td><td>Shinlord&#x27;s Oathblade<br>Heart of the Living Guk<br>Reedwoven Watcher Boots</td></tr><tr><td>gukbottom / 50</td><td>Ghoul Lord&#x27;s Last Decree<br>Pall of the Silent Court<br>Seal of Released Souls</td></tr><tr><td>mistmoore / 40</td><td>Xicotl&#x27;s Midnight Talon<br>Mistmoore Bloodless Gorget<br>Echo of the Unfinished Waltz</td></tr><tr><td>kedge / 50</td><td>Phinigel&#x27;s Tidebound Trident<br>Pearl of the Drowned Chorus<br>Kedge Deepcurrent Robe</td></tr><tr><td>paw / 40</td><td>Ishva&#x27;s Splitpaw Knuckles<br>Splitpaw Spiritcord<br>Denfather Stoneguard</td></tr><tr><td>hole / 50</td><td>Wretched Stonecleaver<br>Pael Sealed Memory<br>Earthbound Oathplate</td></tr><tr><td>qcat / 20</td><td>Omorb&#x27;s Sluicefang<br>Catacomb Vigil Lantern<br>Qeynos Underway Satchel</td></tr><tr><td>fearplane / 50</td><td>Spine of the Faceless<br>Visage of Unbroken Will<br>Dreadhusk of the Last Stand</td></tr><tr><td>hateplane / 50</td><td>Innoruuk&#x27;s Severed Covenant<br>Maestro&#x27;s Unfinished Requiem<br>Seal of the First Betrayal</td></tr><tr><td>airplane / 50</td><td>Veeshan&#x27;s Unwritten Horizon<br>Mantle of the First Brood<br>Astrolabe of the Eighth Island</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Planar relics</h3><p><strong>Fear:</strong> Visage of Unbroken Will reveals the unseen with See Invisible, beside Spine of the Faceless and Dreadhusk of the Last Stand. Its reuse is five minutes.</p><p><strong>Hate:</strong> Maestro’s Unfinished Requiem grants Invisibility; Innoruuk’s Severed Covenant and Seal of the First Betrayal recall hatred and broken elven royalty. Its reuse is ten minutes.</p><p><strong>Sky:</strong> Astrolabe of the Eighth Island grants ordinary Levitate, beside Veeshan’s Unwritten Horizon and Mantle of the First Brood. Its reuse is fifteen minutes. Levitate requires one Bat Wing and respects no-levitation zones, including Sky itself; island keys are still required.</p><p>Each click requires equipping the item at level 46 and a ten-second cast. Both qualities and duplicate copies share the same family cooldown; Ascended does not improve the utility. Cast/reuse figures are base values subject to native focus reductions. Native targeting, reagent conservation and spell restrictions remain.</p><h2 id=\"rewards\">Shared rewards and exclusive drops</h2><p>Twenty-four shared designs include eight armor pieces, eight weapon families, six accessories and two weight-reduction bags. Every dungeon uses these designs at its equipment band. Original dungeons: Befallen 20; Unrest/Najena 30; High Keep/Cazic-Thule 40; Permafrost/Nagafen’s Lair 50. Selection does not filter by class. Rewards are permanent, tradeable, non-lore and have zero merchant resale. Dungeon rewards cannot be converted by existing forging recipes.</p><p>Raid final bosses also drop one, two or three distinct exclusive designs with 80%, 18% and 2% chances. Each independently rolls Polished or Ascended at 90%/10%. Examples include Moltor’s Graveblade, Rucksif’s Mourning Mantle, McCabe’s Hidden Treasury, Vox’s Hoarfrost Satchel and Nagafen’s Emberfang. These shared corpse drops use normal loot controls and are additional to native loot and personal completion rewards.</p><p>Weapon delay stays fixed between qualities. Bags have six, eight or ten slots and up to 100% weight reduction. Rewards are selected durably; reconnecting cannot change them. There is one personal completion reward per character per run. A full inventory leaves an earned claim at the Keeper.</p>\n<h2 id=\"recovery\">Keep progress through interruptions</h2><p>Progress and the original deadline survive reconnects and restarts. Abandoning the task removes its display, not earned credit. Only the creator can confirm a reset, and no player, pending entry or recoverable player corpse may remain inside. Earned claims survive reset and expiry. Classic Cazic-Thule restoration applies only to managed private instances; High Keep keeps normal faction consequences.</p>\n<h2 id=\"testing\">Testing still required</h2><p>All 21 dungeons in both modes need in-game checks. Cazic-Thule paths and doors, inventory/loot recovery and demanding solo/small-group balance remain open. Lady Vox and Lord Nagafen explicitly require level-50 gameplay acceptance. The equipment index covers the separate zone-hunt catalog; dungeon rewards use the designs and bands described here. Existing forging recipes do not upgrade these rewards.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Chapterhouse adds a level-50 Raid/Grind expedition with four named enemies and a separate personal Paladin story journal. There are now 22 dungeon choices: the 21 Classic dungeons plus this curated exception. Six final Raid variants bring the dungeon reward definitions to 420. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — every Classic dungeon:</strong> The installed release extends Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset to 21 Classic combat dungeons, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 dungeons and their new rewards are installed for testing. In-game and balance acceptance are pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon — live testing</h2><p><strong>Live testing.</strong> Added zones: blackburrow, crushbone, runnyeye, soldunga, guktop, gukbottom, mistmoore, kedge, paw, hole, qcat, fearplane, hateplane, airplane. Current native populations are retained; this is not a historical restoration of every zone. Runs keep the existing twelve-hour limit and personal credit requirements.</p><p>Added Raid final bosses receive three dungeon-specific exclusive designs in Polished and Ascended versions. All dungeon rewards are MAGIC; existing item IDs and other stats remain unchanged. Managed Sky adds durable key exchangers on each key island, still requiring the normal tokens. Managed Grind gives the four previously scripted Sky bosses eight-hour timers and preserves the princess’s four-hour timer. Public and legacy Sky retain their original behavior. Plane runs isolate their quest state from public zones and other runs.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Keeper placement — live testing:</strong> The overlapping Keepers in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair now have positions 15 units from their waypoints. High Keep and Cazic-Thule already had separate positions and remain unchanged. Visibility is not yet confirmed in game. If an eye is still hidden, use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail. Waypoints and dungeon progress are unchanged.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Befallen</td><td><code>-67,35,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Unrest</td><td><code>-38,67,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Najena</td><td><code>-61,858,4.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Permafrost</td><td><code>-121,46,2.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Nagafen’s Lair</td><td><code>-424,-248,-108</code></td></tr><tr><td>High Keep (unchanged)</td><td><code>-16,88,4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cazic-Thule (unchanged)</td><td><code>71,-74,4</code></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected dungeon equipment budgets are raised so comparable Normal rewards exceed Ascended starter gear. Modes, objectives, Keepers and eligibility remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. Existing legacy runs keep their original behavior until expiry or reset. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>Raid and Grind choices are available in all 21 Classic combat dungeons listed here, including Fear, Hate and Sky. Each run lasts twelve hours and allows up to six characters. Testing and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"modes\">Choose a mode</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Grind</th><th>Raid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Enemies</td><td>Normal stats and respawns</td><td>35% more HP, 15% more damage; defeated enemies do not return</td></tr><tr><td>Bosses</td><td>Required bosses available initially</td><td>Final boss unlocks after all required minibosses</td></tr><tr><td>Personal reward</td><td>One Normal item</td><td>One item: 90% Polished, 10% Ascended</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"credit\">Earn your own checklist</h2><p>The creator chooses the mode. Hail the entrance Keeper for Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset. Open Tasks and select your dungeon and mode for its checklist and deadline. Keeper Status lists every required boss, your personal credit and permanent completion counts. A yellow Task Stage Completed message marks one boss objective. A full dungeon clear requires personal credit for every required boss. During live testing, if the task objectives are blank or Completed history is missing, use Keeper Status; these display problems do not erase earned credit or rewards. Stay enrolled, connected and within 200 units of your party’s encounter, including vertical distance. Owned-pet kills count for the owner’s party. Missed kills never receive retroactive credit. Grind respawns offer another opportunity; Raid deaths are permanent for that run.</p>\n<h2 id=\"required-bosses\">Required bosses</h2><p>Each name below is required for personal completion in either mode. The final boss is marked; Raid unlocks it after the required minibosses. A group’s unlock does not give missed personal credit.</p><h3>Befallen</h3><ul><li>skeleton Lrodd</li><li>Priest Amiaz</li><li>the thaumaturgist</li><li>Boondin Babbinsbort</li><li>Gynok Moltor — final boss</li></ul><h3>Unrest</h3><ul><li>lesser blade fiend</li><li>a reanimated hand</li><li>reclusive ghoul magus</li><li>an undead barkeep</li><li>an undead knight of Unrest</li><li>a priest of najena</li><li>Garanel Rucksif — final boss</li></ul><h3>High Keep</h3><ul><li>Captain Bosec</li><li>Captain Boshinko</li><li>Dyrna Nlith</li><li>Carson McCabe — final boss</li></ul><h3>Najena</h3><ul><li>Moosh</li><li>Ekeros</li><li>BoneCracker</li><li>Rathyl</li><li>Trazdon</li><li>Drelzna</li><li>the guard captain</li><li>The Widowmistress</li><li>Najena — final boss</li></ul><h3>Cazic-Thule</h3><ul><li>Radiant</li><li>Tae Ew Diviner</li><li>Tae Ew Templar</li><li>Tae Ew Archon</li><li>Cazic Cenobite</li><li>Avatar of Fear — final boss</li></ul><h3>Permafrost</h3><ul><li>a goblin jailmaster</li><li>a goblin preacher</li><li>a goblin scryer</li><li>the goblin sage</li><li>an elite honor guard</li><li>High Priest Zaharn</li><li>King Thex`Ka IV</li><li>Lady Vox — final boss</li></ul><h3>Nagafen’s Lair</h3><ul><li>guano harvester</li><li>kobold noble</li><li>kobold champion</li><li>kobold priest</li><li>Solusek kobold king</li><li>death beetle</li><li>noxious spider</li><li>stone spider</li><li>Efreeti Lord Djarn</li><li>Magus Rokyl</li><li>King Tranix</li><li>Warlord Skarlon</li><li>Lord Nagafen — final boss</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"added-keepers\">Additional entrance Keepers</h2><p>Use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail if its eye model is difficult to select. Locations use in-game <code>/loc</code> order. Hate’s public Keeper is in East Commonlands; its private instances retain the entrance Keeper. Each Keeper has Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blackburrow</td><td><code>-159,23,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Crushbone</td><td><code>-644,174,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Runnyeye</td><td><code>106,201,3.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Solusek&#x27;s Eye</td><td><code>-487.312,-474.688,71.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Upper Guk</td><td><code>-36,23,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Lower Guk</td><td><code>1197,-201,-81.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Mistmoore</td><td><code>-314,120,-179.938</code></td></tr><tr><td>Kedge Keep</td><td><code>100,30,301.875</code></td></tr><tr><td>Splitpaw</td><td><code>-106,63,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>The Hole</td><td><code>624,-1050,-78.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Qeynos Catacombs</td><td><code>860,96,-39.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Fear</td><td><code>-1139,1298,-0.371</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Hate (East Commonlands)</td><td><code>-1570,-346,3</code>; private Hate entrance: <code>-374.8,-337.08,2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Sky</td><td><code>1415,630,-666.709</code></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id=\"added-objectives\">Required bosses in the added dungeons</h2><p>Every listed boss requires personal credit. Raid unlocks the final boss after all required minibosses; Keeper Status is the live checklist.</p><h3>Blackburrow</h3><ul><li>a gnoll commander</li><li>Splitpaw Commander</li><li>the gnoll high shaman</li><li>Lord Elgnub — final boss</li></ul><h3>Crushbone</h3><ul><li>orc taskmaster</li><li>orc warlord</li><li>Lord Darish</li><li>The Prophet</li><li>Ambassador DVinn</li><li>Emperor Crush — final boss</li></ul><h3>Runnyeye</h3><ul><li>The Sporali Moldmaster</li><li>Sludge Dankmire</li><li>Battlelord Paluk</li><li>Battlewizard Unak</li><li>Lord Pickclaw — final boss</li></ul><h3>Solusek&#x27;s Eye</h3><ul><li>flame goblin foreman</li><li>reckless efreeti</li><li>Singe</li><li>Kindle</li><li>inferno goblin captain</li><li>goblin high shaman</li><li>Lord Gimblox</li><li>Solusek goblin king — final boss</li></ul><h3>Upper Guk</h3><ul><li>a froglok gaz squire</li><li>a giant heart spider</li><li>a froglok scryer</li><li>a froglok realist</li><li>the froglok warden</li><li>a froglok summoner</li><li>the froglok shin lord — final boss</li></ul><h3>Lower Guk</h3><ul><li>a minotaur elder</li><li>a minotaur patriarch</li><li>a ghoul supplier</li><li>a ghoul executioner</li><li>a ghoul assassin</li><li>a ghoul sage</li><li>a ghoul cavalier</li><li>a frenzied ghoul</li><li>the ghoul arch magus</li><li>the froglok king</li><li>the ghoul lord — final boss</li></ul><h3>Mistmoore</h3><ul><li>a glyphed ghoul</li><li>an avenging caitiff</li><li>a cloaked dhampyre</li><li>Butler Syncall</li><li>Maid Issis</li><li>Mynthi Davissi</li><li>Lasna Cheroon</li><li>Garton Viswin</li><li>Xicotl — final boss</li></ul><h3>Kedge Keep</h3><ul><li>a frenzied cauldron shark</li><li>a fierce impaler</li><li>Coralyn Kelpmaiden</li><li>Shellara Ebbhunter</li><li>a seahorse matriarch</li><li>a seahorse patriarch</li><li>Cauldronboil</li><li>Undertow</li><li>Priestess Auraia</li><li>Phinigel Autropos — final boss</li></ul><h3>Splitpaw</h3><ul><li>Verishe Mal Judge</li><li>Verishe Mal Executioner</li><li>Tesch Val Kadvem</li><li>Nisch Val Torash Mashk</li><li>Rosch Val L`Vlor</li><li>Tesch Val Deval`Nmak</li><li>The Ishva Mal — final boss</li></ul><h3>The Hole</h3><ul><li>Stonesoul the Unmoving</li><li>Ikurenm the Sly</li><li>Tzitzi the Crazed</li><li>Commander Yarik</li><li>Irslak the Wretched — final boss</li></ul><h3>Qeynos Catacombs</h3><ul><li>a gelatinous cube</li><li>a thug leader</li><li>a ring leader</li><li>a shark</li><li>Omorb — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Fear</h3><ul><li>Dread</li><li>Terror</li><li>Fright</li><li>a dracoliche</li><li>Cazic Thule — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Hate</h3><ul><li>Magi P`Tasa</li><li>Hand of the Maestro</li><li>Maestro of Rancor</li><li>Innoruuk — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Sky</h3><ul><li>a thunder spirit princess</li><li>Protector of Sky</li><li>Gorgalosk</li><li>Keeper of Souls</li><li>The Spiroc Guardian</li><li>The Spiroc Lord</li><li>Bazzt Zzzt</li><li>Sister of the Spire</li><li>Eye of Veeshan — final boss</li></ul><h2 id=\"unique-rewards\">Unique Classic raid rewards — live testing</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p><p>New recommended levels follow each dungeon’s equipment band. Planar items require level 46. All remain permanent, tradeable, non-LORE, zero-resale and outside existing forging recipes. The original seven exclusive families remain, with MAGIC added where needed. Already earned rewards and generated loot keep their identities.</p><p>New numeric power stays within the existing band, slot and quality budgets. Their lore is original Nightcap fiction inspired by each dungeon. Each family has Polished and Ascended versions.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon / band</th><th>Exclusive designs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>blackburrow / 20</td><td>Elgnub&#x27;s Burrowfang<br>Blackburrow Packwarden Mantle<br>Brewer&#x27;s Amber Seal</td></tr><tr><td>crushbone / 20</td><td>Crush&#x27;s Broken Scepter<br>Ambassador&#x27;s Ashen Veil<br>Liberator of the Pens</td></tr><tr><td>runnyeye / 30</td><td>Pickclaw Tunnelbreaker<br>Evil Eye Witness<br>Crown of the Pickclaw Court</td></tr><tr><td>soldunga / 40</td><td>Goblin King&#x27;s Cinderstaff<br>Firebloom Forgegrips<br>Embervault Reliquary</td></tr><tr><td>guktop / 30</td><td>Shinlord&#x27;s Oathblade<br>Heart of the Living Guk<br>Reedwoven Watcher Boots</td></tr><tr><td>gukbottom / 50</td><td>Ghoul Lord&#x27;s Last Decree<br>Pall of the Silent Court<br>Seal of Released Souls</td></tr><tr><td>mistmoore / 40</td><td>Xicotl&#x27;s Midnight Talon<br>Mistmoore Bloodless Gorget<br>Echo of the Unfinished Waltz</td></tr><tr><td>kedge / 50</td><td>Phinigel&#x27;s Tidebound Trident<br>Pearl of the Drowned Chorus<br>Kedge Deepcurrent Robe</td></tr><tr><td>paw / 40</td><td>Ishva&#x27;s Splitpaw Knuckles<br>Splitpaw Spiritcord<br>Denfather Stoneguard</td></tr><tr><td>hole / 50</td><td>Wretched Stonecleaver<br>Pael Sealed Memory<br>Earthbound Oathplate</td></tr><tr><td>qcat / 20</td><td>Omorb&#x27;s Sluicefang<br>Catacomb Vigil Lantern<br>Qeynos Underway Satchel</td></tr><tr><td>fearplane / 50</td><td>Spine of the Faceless<br>Visage of Unbroken Will<br>Dreadhusk of the Last Stand</td></tr><tr><td>hateplane / 50</td><td>Innoruuk&#x27;s Severed Covenant<br>Maestro&#x27;s Unfinished Requiem<br>Seal of the First Betrayal</td></tr><tr><td>airplane / 50</td><td>Veeshan&#x27;s Unwritten Horizon<br>Mantle of the First Brood<br>Astrolabe of the Eighth Island</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Planar relics</h3><p><strong>Fear:</strong> Visage of Unbroken Will reveals the unseen with See Invisible, beside Spine of the Faceless and Dreadhusk of the Last Stand. Its reuse is five minutes.</p><p><strong>Hate:</strong> Maestro’s Unfinished Requiem grants Invisibility; Innoruuk’s Severed Covenant and Seal of the First Betrayal recall hatred and broken elven royalty. Its reuse is ten minutes.</p><p><strong>Sky:</strong> Astrolabe of the Eighth Island grants ordinary Levitate, beside Veeshan’s Unwritten Horizon and Mantle of the First Brood. Its reuse is fifteen minutes. Levitate requires one Bat Wing and respects no-levitation zones, including Sky itself; island keys are still required.</p><p>Each click requires equipping the item at level 46 and a ten-second cast. Both qualities and duplicate copies share the same family cooldown; Ascended does not improve the utility. Cast/reuse figures are base values subject to native focus reductions. Native targeting, reagent conservation and spell restrictions remain.</p><h2 id=\"rewards\">Shared rewards and exclusive drops</h2><p>Twenty-four shared designs include eight armor pieces, eight weapon families, six accessories and two weight-reduction bags. Every dungeon uses these designs at its equipment band. Original dungeons: Befallen 20; Unrest/Najena 30; High Keep/Cazic-Thule 40; Permafrost/Nagafen’s Lair 50. Selection does not filter by class. Rewards are permanent, tradeable, non-lore and have zero merchant resale. Dungeon rewards cannot be converted by existing forging recipes.</p><p>Raid final bosses also drop one, two or three distinct exclusive designs with 80%, 18% and 2% chances. Each independently rolls Polished or Ascended at 90%/10%. Examples include Moltor’s Graveblade, Rucksif’s Mourning Mantle, McCabe’s Hidden Treasury, Vox’s Hoarfrost Satchel and Nagafen’s Emberfang. These shared corpse drops use normal loot controls and are additional to native loot and personal completion rewards.</p><p>Weapon delay stays fixed between qualities. Bags have six, eight or ten slots and up to 100% weight reduction. Rewards are selected durably; reconnecting cannot change them. There is one personal completion reward per character per run. A full inventory leaves an earned claim at the Keeper.</p>\n<h2 id=\"recovery\">Keep progress through interruptions</h2><p>Progress and the original deadline survive reconnects and restarts. Abandoning the task removes its display, not earned credit. Only the creator can confirm a reset, and no player, pending entry or recoverable player corpse may remain inside. Earned claims survive reset and expiry. Classic Cazic-Thule restoration applies only to managed private instances; High Keep keeps normal faction consequences.</p>\n<h2 id=\"testing\">Testing still required</h2><p>All 21 dungeons in both modes need in-game checks. Cazic-Thule paths and doors, inventory/loot recovery and demanding solo/small-group balance remain open. Lady Vox and Lord Nagafen explicitly require level-50 gameplay acceptance. The equipment index covers the separate zone-hunt catalog; dungeon rewards use the designs and bands described here. Existing forging recipes do not upgrade these rewards.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Chapterhouse adds a level-50 Raid/Grind expedition with four named enemies and a separate personal Paladin story journal. There are now 22 dungeon choices: the 21 Classic dungeons plus this curated exception. Six final Raid variants bring the dungeon reward definitions to 420. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — not released</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is a prepared level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. It is not yet installed. Client appearance and complete encounters still require in-game acceptance.</p><p>Four bosses, personal credit and Raid/Grind journals follow the existing expedition system. The separate story has fourteen objectives and durable progress. Temporary war souls give no loot or XP.</p>",
