   "slug": "item-upgrades",
   "title": "Item upgrades",
   "summary": "Turn matching copies into a higher quality, with the right recipe for each system.",
-  "body": "<h2 id=\"quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p><a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Ordinary quality variants can satisfy Normal quest requirements</a>. This does not change the number or quality of copies required by the Reforging Box or zone forging.</p>\n<h2 id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The update changes stats on existing ordinary qualities. It does not change forge costs, quality chances, recipes or item ownership. Reforging still uses the existing progression.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended values and intermediate stats have been retuned while retaining item identities, effects and sockets. Upgrade costs, commands and existing ownership are unchanged.</p>\n<p>Nightcap has two forgeable tier families: ordinary tiered equipment ends at <strong>Ascended</strong>, while the Classic zone-hunt rewards end at <strong>Ascension</strong>. They have separate item definitions. Match the exact item and quality.</p>\n<h2 id=\"recipes\">Upgrade recipes</h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><caption>Guaranteed upgrades with no coin fee</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Input</th><th scope=\"col\">Result</th><th scope=\"col\">Method</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">3 identical eligible Normal/Base copies</th><td>1 Polished</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Polished copies</th><td>1 Exalted</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Exalted copies</th><td>1 Ascended ordinary item, or 1 Ascension zone reward</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"box\">Get the reusable Reforging Box</h2><ol><li>Hail <strong>Artisan Veyra</strong> in the East Commonlands tunnel for a free Reforging Box.</li><li>Put the box in a main inventory slot. Leave combat and casting, empty your cursor, and close trade, loot, merchant and station interactions.</li><li>Place three identical eligible Normal/Base copies (leave one slot empty), or four identical Polished or Exalted copies in the box. This is a container combine, not an NPC hand-in.</li><li>Press Combine. A valid recipe consumes the required copies and gives one next-quality item; keep the box for later.</li></ol><p>The box has no recipe above the top tier. Bags cannot be nested in the box. The supported-item catalog determines eligibility.</p>\n<h2 id=\"normal-items\">Three Normal items make Polished</h2><p>The Reforging Box accepts exactly <strong>3 identical eligible Normal (Base) items → 1 Polished item</strong>, for ordinary tiered equipment and Classic zone-hunt rewards. Put the three copies in the reusable box, leave its fourth slot empty, and press Combine. A matching Polished version must exist. The higher recipes still cost four copies. Stackable units count individually; nonstackable charged items count once each. Dungeon rewards and bags remain excluded. The recipe is available for live testing; in-game acceptance remains ongoing.</p>\n<h2 id=\"requirements\">Before combining</h2><p>Use unmodified items of one family and quality. An item's built-in color is allowed; a different player-applied dye color is not. Socketed, player-dyed, ornamented, customized and evolving instances are not eligible. Binding is preserved. Charged objects count as physical items, not as one copy per charge. If a result is unclear or items appear missing, stop retrying and contact the owner.</p>\n<h2 id=\"other-upgrades\">Keep other systems separate</h2><p><a href=\"ascension.html\">Epic Ascension</a> uses its own quest and materials. <a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Ordinary tradeskills</a> retain recipe requirements and success chances. The top-tier names do not mean those systems share recipes.</p><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Dungeon rewards</a> use Normal, Polished and Ascended qualities but have no conversion through these recipes. Earn their qualities through Grind or Raid completion and Raid final-boss drops.</p>\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Ember of the First Dawn uses #zoneforge: three Base copies or four Polished/Exalted copies make the next quality. Camil’s helmet receives no new socket. The miniboss and final Raid equipment do not use this augment recipe. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p><a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Ordinary quality variants can satisfy Normal quest requirements</a>. This does not change the number or quality of copies required by the Reforging Box or zone forging.</p>\n<h2 id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The update changes stats on existing ordinary qualities. It does not change forge costs, quality chances, recipes or item ownership. Reforging still uses the existing progression.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended values and intermediate stats have been retuned while retaining item identities, effects and sockets. Upgrade costs, commands and existing ownership are unchanged.</p>\n<p>Nightcap has two forgeable tier families: ordinary tiered equipment ends at <strong>Ascended</strong>, while the Classic zone-hunt rewards end at <strong>Ascension</strong>. They have separate item definitions. Match the exact item and quality.</p>\n<h2 id=\"recipes\">Upgrade recipes</h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><caption>Guaranteed upgrades with no coin fee</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Input</th><th scope=\"col\">Result</th><th scope=\"col\">Method</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">3 identical eligible Normal/Base copies</th><td>1 Polished</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Polished copies</th><td>1 Exalted</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Exalted copies</th><td>1 Ascended ordinary item, or 1 Ascension zone reward</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"box\">Get the reusable Reforging Box</h2><ol><li>Hail <strong>Artisan Veyra</strong> in the East Commonlands tunnel for a free Reforging Box.</li><li>Put the box in a main inventory slot. Leave combat and casting, empty your cursor, and close trade, loot, merchant and station interactions.</li><li>Place three identical eligible Normal/Base copies (leave one slot empty), or four identical Polished or Exalted copies in the box. This is a container combine, not an NPC hand-in.</li><li>Press Combine. A valid recipe consumes the required copies and gives one next-quality item; keep the box for later.</li></ol><p>The box has no recipe above the top tier. Bags cannot be nested in the box. The supported-item catalog determines eligibility.</p>\n<h2 id=\"normal-items\">Three Normal items make Polished</h2><p>The Reforging Box accepts exactly <strong>3 identical eligible Normal (Base) items → 1 Polished item</strong>, for ordinary tiered equipment and Classic zone-hunt rewards. Put the three copies in the reusable box, leave its fourth slot empty, and press Combine. A matching Polished version must exist. The higher recipes still cost four copies. Stackable units count individually; nonstackable charged items count once each. Dungeon rewards and bags remain excluded. The recipe is available for live testing; in-game acceptance remains ongoing.</p>\n<h2 id=\"requirements\">Before combining</h2><p>Use unmodified items of one family and quality. An item's built-in color is allowed; a different player-applied dye color is not. Socketed, player-dyed, ornamented, customized and evolving instances are not eligible. Binding is preserved. Charged objects count as physical items, not as one copy per charge. If a result is unclear or items appear missing, stop retrying and contact the owner.</p>\n<h2 id=\"other-upgrades\">Keep other systems separate</h2><p><a href=\"ascension.html\">Epic Ascension</a> uses its own quest and materials. <a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Ordinary tradeskills</a> retain recipe requirements and success chances. The top-tier names do not mean those systems share recipes.</p><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Dungeon rewards</a> use Normal, Polished and Ascended qualities but have no conversion through these recipes. Earn their qualities through Grind or Raid completion and Raid final-boss drops.</p>\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Ember of the First Dawn uses #zoneforge: three Base copies or four Polished/Exalted copies make the next quality. Camil’s helmet receives no new socket. The miniboss and final Raid equipment do not use this augment recipe. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — not released</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is a prepared level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. It is not yet installed. Client appearance and complete encounters still require in-game acceptance.</p><p>Cinder forging uses three identical Base copies, then four Polished or Exalted copies. The helmet and other Kael equipment do not use that augment recipe.</p>",
