-  "body": "<h2 id=\"hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"aa-level-progression\">October 23: two AA per level and level-1 AA controls</h2><p>The paired update is installed for live testing. Keep AA allocation at 0% to earn full leveling XP plus two AA per level. Use the AA +/− controls from level 1, choose an intermediate percentage, or select 100% to hold your level and grind AA. Full focus earns 20 AA per current-level equivalent of XP. Update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Saved points, purchases and partial progress are retained; native gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"loot-finder-preview\">October 22: production loot finder</h2><p>The <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">class and era loot finder</a> supports any held class by default, optional all-class matching, slot/quality/level/zone filters and item links to source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. Production content refreshes automatically every fifteen minutes, with the last successful capture retained if a refresh fails. Existing gameplay, rewards and acceptance labels are unchanged.</p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<h2 id=\"build-lab\">Build Lab — October 22</h2><p>The <a href=\"build-lab.html\">experimental Build Lab</a> compares two saved builds, supported spell benefits, Hunt item stat differences and editable ability priorities. Inspect mana and cast timelines or search the best priority order under your test conditions. It uses dated source controls and explicit assumptions, not a complete native combat simulation or universal best-build ranking.</p>\n<h2 id=\"interactive-handbook\">October 22 — Your interactive field guide</h2><p>The wiki has a new lantern-lit design with four adventure paths, instant quick search, saved guides, light and dark reading modes, and a reading-progress bar. The equipment catalog keeps its filters and all four reward qualities. On the home page, expand <strong>Release notes &amp; live testing</strong> for the existing gameplay notices. <a href=\"about.html#navigation\">Learn the shortcuts and field notes →</a></p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"classic-dungeons-candidate\">October 22 — every Classic dungeon and unique rewards live</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p>The paired release also repairs stale dungeon item checks behind the reported Keeper error and installs durable Sky key services. Existing runs, earned rewards and the latest quest-tier and client updates are preserved. Native gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"quest-ingredients-20261022\">October 22 - quest ingredient fix live for testing</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended ingredients can satisfy Normal quest requirements, including Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. Shared hand-ins, task delivery and five older Temple quests are covered. The paired server and quest release is deployed; player QA remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Scope and limits</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"class-armor-candidate\">October 22 — Ascended class-armor quest rewards</h2><p>Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests now grant 37 reviewed Ascended armor rewards. Substantial repeatable class-armor quests qualify; cheap/basic hand-ins remain excluded. The dependent Darkforge epic turn-in accepts Normal and Ascended pieces. Existing owned gear is not automatically converted. <strong>Live testing:</strong> native delivery and balance acceptance remain open. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Scope and testing</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals — live testing</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"classic-robes-20261022\">October 22 — robe waist correction in live testing</h2><p>Game update <strong>2026102204</strong> repairs the native waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed, covering all seven added Classic robe races and both genders. Close the game, reopen the normal launcher and press Play. In-game visual, dye and animation acceptance remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Read the scope</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"keeper-visibility-20261022\">October 22 — Dungeon Keeper placement</h2><p>The correction now separates Keepers from overlapping waypoints in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. High Keep and Cazic-Thule already had separate positions. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">All seven Keeper locations</a> are listed for live testing; visibility remains unconfirmed. Waypoints, dungeon progress and client files are unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p><h2 id=\"aa-million-xp\">October 21: slower AA earning and XP boost retirement</h2><p>The October 21 release used 1,000,000 AA experience per point with 10% passive earning; the October 23 level-scaled update supersedes that earning model. Goldwind’s paid package is retired, Matron’s free buffs remain, and XP boost durations are respected. Existing points and purchases remain intact. Live balance testing continues.</p>\n<h2 id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"all-class-aa-20261019\">October 19: all-class AA update</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. No existing line is removed. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Launch repair published:</strong> Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update. Close EverQuest and the launcher, reopen your normal Nightcap shortcut, and press Play to receive the repair. Your game settings and the other managed files are preserved. Native login and gameplay confirmation remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"thj-release\">October 18: item, spell, pet and melee release</h2><p><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended items now use reviewed THJ values. Direct damage adds effective Spell Damage, ordinary DoT ticks add half, and heroic INT/WIS improve direct values. Starter quality steps remain modest below comparable Normal dungeon equipment.</p><p>The same release adds paged permanent-pet equipment, bounded owner-stat inheritance, earned pet/melee AA updates, separate Rabid Bear benefit and illusion effects, and shared 750 base caps with Hunt headroom. Close EverQuest and use the launcher for game update 2026101802. Classic level 50 remains active; gameplay and balance acceptance are still open.</p>\n<h2>October 18 - More ordinary quality loot</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended now have 20%, 5% and 1% chances per eligible ordinary equipment/bag drop. Hunt, dungeon and quest rewards are unchanged. Already generated loot is not rerolled.</p><h2 id=\"reforge-colors\">October 18, 2026: built-in item colors</h2><p>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#requirements\">Reforging Box</a> and <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#forging\">zone forging</a> now accept an item's built-in color. This fixes ordinary items such as Dagger of Marnek being rejected as customized. A different player-applied dye color and the other customization restrictions still prevent combining. Recipes remain three Normal/Base copies or four higher-quality copies. No client update is required for this fix; in-game acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"october-18-cooldowns\">October 18, 2026: separate ability cooldowns</h2><p><a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Activated AA families now have independent cooldowns</a>, including Rampage and Purify Body. Item and discipline timer collisions are also repaired. Existing saved waits keep their original expiry. Reconnect and test your abilities; <a href=\"unreleased.html#cooldown-identities\">generic skill and content-defined groups</a> remain under review.</p>\n<h2 id=\"october-18\">October 18, 2026: Classic travel file repair</h2><p>Signed game update 2026101801 adds automatic missing/corrupt terrain and object archive repair for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia. Close EverQuest and press Play in the usual launcher. Existing gameplay assets and player settings are preserved; native zoning acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"october-17\">October 17, 2026: progression, combat and crafting</h2><ul><li>The optional <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> provides an early survival, sustain and damage shortlist across held classes.</li><li>Passive AA is now 10%, preserving full leveling EXP, earned points and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks</a> have separate reuse. <a href=\"combat.html#cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</a> address excessive and restarted timers; other shared identities remain under investigation.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">Normal death costs no EXP or levels</a>; prior losses are not refunded.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html#stack-limits\">Stackable items support at least 100</a>, retaining larger limits.</li><li>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">Reforging Box accepts three identical eligible Normal/Base copies</a> for Polished. Higher recipes still cost four.</li><li>Idle zones can unload without ending their workers and triggering a whole-game restart.</li><li>Update through launcher Play for the matched client. Gameplay and balance acceptance continue.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"october-16\">October 16, 2026</h2><ul><li>The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#required-bosses\">dungeon guide now lists every required boss</a> and explains boss-stage notices, full-clear credit and Keeper Status when task objectives are blank.</li><li><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeons</a> are deployed for live testing with personal boss checklists, shared rewards and exclusive Raid drops. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</li><li><a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> now gathers the major departures from Classic.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Equipment eligibility</a> recognizes held classes and permits playable races when the class matches; remaining restrictions still apply.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Temporary AA buffs</a> retain their timers; ordinary blessings remain lasting.</li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html#banking\">Mira Coinwell</a> provides tunnel banking. Haldra stocks Leather Padding.</li><li>The wiki’s guides, commands and generated reward pages have been reviewed together against current release evidence.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"october-13\">October 13, 2026</h2><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Passive AA changed from 40% to 20%</a>, preserving full normal XP and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#alternate-abilities\">All allowed AA ranks open at level 1</a>; points, eligibility and prerequisite ranks remain.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Stacked tradeskill ingredients and Craft All</a> are deployed.</li><li>The tunnel workshop layout is more spacious; the <a href=\"waypoints.html\">Unrest waypoint</a> moved beside its entrance Keeper.</li><li>Supported divine summoned-hammer families have <a href=\"equipment.html#summoned-gear\">zero resale value</a>.</li><li>The reported multiclass training/offhand issue and merchant Sell All button issue were confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"october-12\">October 11–12, 2026</h2><ul><li><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Reusable four-copy upgrades</a> are available from Artisan Veyra; higher #zoneforge steps now use four copies.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">LORE restrictions are disabled</a>. Food and drink requirements were removed.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Early scribing</a> allows eligible scrolls into the spellbook before their casting level.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#selling\">Sell All protects food, drink, reagents and casting focus items</a>.</li><li>The launcher uses personal access codes and shows <a href=\"launcher.html#patch-notes\">patch summaries</a>.</li><li>Waypoint portals and floating-eye Instance Keepers received visual corrections. The reported pet-summon crash was confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"october-9\">October 9, 2026</h2><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">48 Classic reward zones</a>, <a href=\"items.html\">384 reward variants</a>, type-22 augments and zone forging launched.</li><li>Passive AA increased to 40% at that time; the October 13 reduction above supersedes that rate.</li><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html#row-controls\">Always Loot / Never Loot controls</a>, effective Spell Damage on <a href=\"combat.html#throw-stone\">Throw Stone</a>, and retained spell gems after normal death were added.</li></ul><p>Release labels describe availability, not completed balance or gameplay acceptance. See <a href=\"unreleased.html\">In development</a> for candidates.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>October 23: Camil’s Chapterhouse quest, level-50–53 encounters, custom rewards, Ember augment, waypoint and Keeper are deployed for live testing. Native Tasks track the story. Full encounter balance and player acceptance remain open. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"aa-level-progression\">October 23: two AA per level and level-1 AA controls</h2><p>The paired update is installed for live testing. Keep AA allocation at 0% to earn full leveling XP plus two AA per level. Use the AA +/− controls from level 1, choose an intermediate percentage, or select 100% to hold your level and grind AA. Full focus earns 20 AA per current-level equivalent of XP. Update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Saved points, purchases and partial progress are retained; native gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"loot-finder-preview\">October 22: production loot finder</h2><p>The <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">class and era loot finder</a> supports any held class by default, optional all-class matching, slot/quality/level/zone filters and item links to source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. Production content refreshes automatically every fifteen minutes, with the last successful capture retained if a refresh fails. Existing gameplay, rewards and acceptance labels are unchanged.</p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<h2 id=\"build-lab\">Build Lab — October 22</h2><p>The <a href=\"build-lab.html\">experimental Build Lab</a> compares two saved builds, supported spell benefits, Hunt item stat differences and editable ability priorities. Inspect mana and cast timelines or search the best priority order under your test conditions. It uses dated source controls and explicit assumptions, not a complete native combat simulation or universal best-build ranking.</p>\n<h2 id=\"interactive-handbook\">October 22 — Your interactive field guide</h2><p>The wiki has a new lantern-lit design with four adventure paths, instant quick search, saved guides, light and dark reading modes, and a reading-progress bar. The equipment catalog keeps its filters and all four reward qualities. On the home page, expand <strong>Release notes &amp; live testing</strong> for the existing gameplay notices. <a href=\"about.html#navigation\">Learn the shortcuts and field notes →</a></p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"classic-dungeons-candidate\">October 22 — every Classic dungeon and unique rewards live</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p>The paired release also repairs stale dungeon item checks behind the reported Keeper error and installs durable Sky key services. Existing runs, earned rewards and the latest quest-tier and client updates are preserved. Native gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"quest-ingredients-20261022\">October 22 - quest ingredient fix live for testing</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended ingredients can satisfy Normal quest requirements, including Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. Shared hand-ins, task delivery and five older Temple quests are covered. The paired server and quest release is deployed; player QA remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Scope and limits</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"class-armor-candidate\">October 22 — Ascended class-armor quest rewards</h2><p>Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests now grant 37 reviewed Ascended armor rewards. Substantial repeatable class-armor quests qualify; cheap/basic hand-ins remain excluded. The dependent Darkforge epic turn-in accepts Normal and Ascended pieces. Existing owned gear is not automatically converted. <strong>Live testing:</strong> native delivery and balance acceptance remain open. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Scope and testing</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals — live testing</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"classic-robes-20261022\">October 22 — robe waist correction in live testing</h2><p>Game update <strong>2026102204</strong> repairs the native waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed, covering all seven added Classic robe races and both genders. Close the game, reopen the normal launcher and press Play. In-game visual, dye and animation acceptance remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Read the scope</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"keeper-visibility-20261022\">October 22 — Dungeon Keeper placement</h2><p>The correction now separates Keepers from overlapping waypoints in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. High Keep and Cazic-Thule already had separate positions. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">All seven Keeper locations</a> are listed for live testing; visibility remains unconfirmed. Waypoints, dungeon progress and client files are unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p><h2 id=\"aa-million-xp\">October 21: slower AA earning and XP boost retirement</h2><p>The October 21 release used 1,000,000 AA experience per point with 10% passive earning; the October 23 level-scaled update supersedes that earning model. Goldwind’s paid package is retired, Matron’s free buffs remain, and XP boost durations are respected. Existing points and purchases remain intact. Live balance testing continues.</p>\n<h2 id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"all-class-aa-20261019\">October 19: all-class AA update</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. No existing line is removed. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Launch repair published:</strong> Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update. Close EverQuest and the launcher, reopen your normal Nightcap shortcut, and press Play to receive the repair. Your game settings and the other managed files are preserved. Native login and gameplay confirmation remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"thj-release\">October 18: item, spell, pet and melee release</h2><p><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended items now use reviewed THJ values. Direct damage adds effective Spell Damage, ordinary DoT ticks add half, and heroic INT/WIS improve direct values. Starter quality steps remain modest below comparable Normal dungeon equipment.</p><p>The same release adds paged permanent-pet equipment, bounded owner-stat inheritance, earned pet/melee AA updates, separate Rabid Bear benefit and illusion effects, and shared 750 base caps with Hunt headroom. Close EverQuest and use the launcher for game update 2026101802. Classic level 50 remains active; gameplay and balance acceptance are still open.</p>\n<h2>October 18 - More ordinary quality loot</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended now have 20%, 5% and 1% chances per eligible ordinary equipment/bag drop. Hunt, dungeon and quest rewards are unchanged. Already generated loot is not rerolled.</p><h2 id=\"reforge-colors\">October 18, 2026: built-in item colors</h2><p>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#requirements\">Reforging Box</a> and <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#forging\">zone forging</a> now accept an item's built-in color. This fixes ordinary items such as Dagger of Marnek being rejected as customized. A different player-applied dye color and the other customization restrictions still prevent combining. Recipes remain three Normal/Base copies or four higher-quality copies. No client update is required for this fix; in-game acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"october-18-cooldowns\">October 18, 2026: separate ability cooldowns</h2><p><a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Activated AA families now have independent cooldowns</a>, including Rampage and Purify Body. Item and discipline timer collisions are also repaired. Existing saved waits keep their original expiry. Reconnect and test your abilities; <a href=\"unreleased.html#cooldown-identities\">generic skill and content-defined groups</a> remain under review.</p>\n<h2 id=\"october-18\">October 18, 2026: Classic travel file repair</h2><p>Signed game update 2026101801 adds automatic missing/corrupt terrain and object archive repair for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia. Close EverQuest and press Play in the usual launcher. Existing gameplay assets and player settings are preserved; native zoning acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"october-17\">October 17, 2026: progression, combat and crafting</h2><ul><li>The optional <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> provides an early survival, sustain and damage shortlist across held classes.</li><li>Passive AA is now 10%, preserving full leveling EXP, earned points and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks</a> have separate reuse. <a href=\"combat.html#cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</a> address excessive and restarted timers; other shared identities remain under investigation.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">Normal death costs no EXP or levels</a>; prior losses are not refunded.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html#stack-limits\">Stackable items support at least 100</a>, retaining larger limits.</li><li>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">Reforging Box accepts three identical eligible Normal/Base copies</a> for Polished. Higher recipes still cost four.</li><li>Idle zones can unload without ending their workers and triggering a whole-game restart.</li><li>Update through launcher Play for the matched client. Gameplay and balance acceptance continue.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"october-16\">October 16, 2026</h2><ul><li>The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#required-bosses\">dungeon guide now lists every required boss</a> and explains boss-stage notices, full-clear credit and Keeper Status when task objectives are blank.</li><li><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeons</a> are deployed for live testing with personal boss checklists, shared rewards and exclusive Raid drops. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</li><li><a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> now gathers the major departures from Classic.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Equipment eligibility</a> recognizes held classes and permits playable races when the class matches; remaining restrictions still apply.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Temporary AA buffs</a> retain their timers; ordinary blessings remain lasting.</li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html#banking\">Mira Coinwell</a> provides tunnel banking. Haldra stocks Leather Padding.</li><li>The wiki’s guides, commands and generated reward pages have been reviewed together against current release evidence.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"october-13\">October 13, 2026</h2><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Passive AA changed from 40% to 20%</a>, preserving full normal XP and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#alternate-abilities\">All allowed AA ranks open at level 1</a>; points, eligibility and prerequisite ranks remain.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Stacked tradeskill ingredients and Craft All</a> are deployed.</li><li>The tunnel workshop layout is more spacious; the <a href=\"waypoints.html\">Unrest waypoint</a> moved beside its entrance Keeper.</li><li>Supported divine summoned-hammer families have <a href=\"equipment.html#summoned-gear\">zero resale value</a>.</li><li>The reported multiclass training/offhand issue and merchant Sell All button issue were confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"october-12\">October 11–12, 2026</h2><ul><li><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Reusable four-copy upgrades</a> are available from Artisan Veyra; higher #zoneforge steps now use four copies.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">LORE restrictions are disabled</a>. Food and drink requirements were removed.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Early scribing</a> allows eligible scrolls into the spellbook before their casting level.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#selling\">Sell All protects food, drink, reagents and casting focus items</a>.</li><li>The launcher uses personal access codes and shows <a href=\"launcher.html#patch-notes\">patch summaries</a>.</li><li>Waypoint portals and floating-eye Instance Keepers received visual corrections. The reported pet-summon crash was confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"october-9\">October 9, 2026</h2><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">48 Classic reward zones</a>, <a href=\"items.html\">384 reward variants</a>, type-22 augments and zone forging launched.</li><li>Passive AA increased to 40% at that time; the October 13 reduction above supersedes that rate.</li><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html#row-controls\">Always Loot / Never Loot controls</a>, effective Spell Damage on <a href=\"combat.html#throw-stone\">Throw Stone</a>, and retained spell gems after normal death were added.</li></ul><p>Release labels describe availability, not completed balance or gameplay acceptance. See <a href=\"unreleased.html\">In development</a> for candidates.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>October 23: Camil’s Chapterhouse quest, level-50–53 encounters, custom rewards, Ember augment, waypoint and Keeper are deployed for live testing. Native Tasks track the story. Full encounter balance and player acceptance remain open. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — not released</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is a prepared level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. It is not yet installed. Client appearance and complete encounters still require in-game acceptance.</p>",
