   "slug": "waypoints",
   "title": "Waypoint Explorer",
   "summary": "Discover return destinations and earn the Explorer title.",
-  "body": "<h2 id=\"crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals — live testing</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n<p>Explore the world, unlock return destinations, and earn a title.</p>\n        <ul class=\"quest-facts\"><li><strong>Start:</strong> Approach a marker named <strong>a waypoint</strong>. The Waypoint Master in the tunnel explains your progress.</li><li><strong>Goal:</strong> Discover every waypoint shown in your current progress by approaching its marker.</li><li><strong>Rewards:</strong> Each discovery unlocks a return destination with the Waypoint Master. Completing the current catalog unlocks the title <strong>the Explorer</strong>.</li><li><strong>How it tracks:</strong> Discoveries are saved per character. Progress is tracked through discovery and NPC dialogue.</li></ul><p>See <a href=\"tunnel.html\">the tunnel guide</a> for services and <a href=\"travel.html\">travel options</a> for your next destination.</p><h2 id=\"markers\">Recognize the crystal and Keeper</h2><p>The waypoint is a crystal with a portal effect and an <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. The glow depends on particle settings; the added model still needs particles-off testing. A nearby small floating eye is the separate Instance Keeper. At Unrest, the portal and recall destination are beside the entrance Keeper at <code>/loc -38, 52, 3</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Chapterhouse has a waypoint that recalls to its public service foyer. Its Keeper controls admission to private runs. Register the waypoint there before recalling to it. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals — live testing</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n<p>Explore the world, unlock return destinations, and earn a title.</p>\n        <ul class=\"quest-facts\"><li><strong>Start:</strong> Approach a marker named <strong>a waypoint</strong>. The Waypoint Master in the tunnel explains your progress.</li><li><strong>Goal:</strong> Discover every waypoint shown in your current progress by approaching its marker.</li><li><strong>Rewards:</strong> Each discovery unlocks a return destination with the Waypoint Master. Completing the current catalog unlocks the title <strong>the Explorer</strong>.</li><li><strong>How it tracks:</strong> Discoveries are saved per character. Progress is tracked through discovery and NPC dialogue.</li></ul><p>See <a href=\"tunnel.html\">the tunnel guide</a> for services and <a href=\"travel.html\">travel options</a> for your next destination.</p><h2 id=\"markers\">Recognize the crystal and Keeper</h2><p>The waypoint is a crystal with a portal effect and an <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. The glow depends on particle settings; the added model still needs particles-off testing. A nearby small floating eye is the separate Instance Keeper. At Unrest, the portal and recall destination are beside the entrance Keeper at <code>/loc -38, 52, 3</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Chapterhouse has a waypoint that recalls to its public service foyer. Its Keeper controls admission to private runs. Register the waypoint there before recalling to it. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — not released</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is a prepared level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. It is not yet installed. Client appearance and complete encounters still require in-game acceptance.</p><p>The Kael waypoint recalls to its public foyer. It does not enter someone else’s private expedition.</p>",
